    "notes": "The strength index data shows a stalling pattern across the board this period. Chest made a marginal gain of 1 point (104 to 105), and shoulders also nudged up 1 point (101 to 102), but neither meets the 3-point threshold that would qualify as on-track progress. Back held completely flat at 103, and triceps and biceps were also unchanged at 104 and 101 respectively. Most notably, legs actually regressed by 1 point, dropping from 108 to 107. While a 1-point drop does not trigger the regression classification, it is a directional concern given that legs were previously the strongest-trending group. No muscle group met the criteria for on-track progress, which is why this period is classified as stalling. The previous period's note flagged steady progress on main lifts and advised watching recovery — it now appears that recovery or stimulus variety may be the limiting factor.",
