    "Prioritize leg training this week: consider adding a set to your leg work or reordering your sessions so legs are trained when you are freshest, as the slight strength index dip there suggests it may be receiving lower quality effort.",
    "Review your recovery habits — the previous period's note flagged this, and a stalling strength index across nearly all groups is consistent with insufficient sleep, nutrition, or rest days undermining your adaptation.",
    "Bring biceps volume closer in line with triceps by adding one additional biceps set, or increase the load on existing sets, to address the emerging elbow flexor-to-extensor imbalance before it becomes more pronounced."
  ],
  "contextSummary": "Strength index stalled across all major muscle groups this period (chest +1, shoulders +1, back/biceps/triceps flat, legs -1), with 28 sets and 10,732 kg tonnage logged; priority for next period is breaking the plateau via load progression, stronger leg focus, and recovery review."
